2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: CONCLUSION:
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: The giant-MCE effect is real and large when the material is operated within
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: its own narrow first-order transition window -- but Gd5Si2Ge2's window sits
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: ~5K below the ASHRAE data-center range, so it is not directly
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: usable for this application as-is. This does not overturn the
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: conclusion (Gd trails vapor-compression/liquid cooling on COP within the
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: ASHRAE range). What it DOES support: literature confirms the Gd5(SixGe1-x)4
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: family has composition-tunable ordering temperature (Pecharsky & Gschneidner,
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: Appl. Phys. Lett. 70, 3299 (1997), report tunability from ~30K to ~276K by
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: Si:Ge ratio, with Gd5Si4 itself ordering at ~335K) -- so a composition between
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: Gd5Si2Ge2 and Gd5Si4 tuned to ~291-300K, IF it retains first-order/giant
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: character at that composition, is the genuinely promising untested direction
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: for closing the COP gap. This is a materials-synthesis question outside what
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: a simulation study alone can answer and remains an open materials
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: research question rather than a result established here.
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: For reference, baselines at this operating point: VCC COP=12.22, Liquid COP=19.89
2026-09-04 18:39:49 [INFO   ] main: Note also: even correctly targeted, Gd5Si2Ge2's COP_electrical (5.29) is close to Gd's own COP_electrical at its matched point (5.00), not dramatically higher, despite ~4x the cooling capacity (Qc). This is consistent with the Sobol sensitivity analysis: COP_electrical is driven mainly by frequency/flow/field-dependent losses (loss_model.py), not by which material is loaded into the regenerator -- a bigger MCE mostly buys more Qc per kg, not a better COP.
