2026-09-04 18:40:29 [INFO   ] main: Interpretation: with the state-dependent loss model (eddy ~ f²H²,
2026-09-04 18:40:29 [INFO   ] main: pump ~ mdot^2, base overhead ~ Qc) in place of the constant
2026-09-04 18:40:29 [INFO   ] main: parasitic_fraction, mu0H_max/frequency/fluid_mdot now carry real
2026-09-04 18:40:29 [INFO   ] main: sensitivity in COP_electrical, because raising frequency or field no
2026-09-04 18:40:29 [INFO   ] main: longer only raises Qc for free -- it also raises the eddy-current loss
2026-09-04 18:40:29 [INFO   ] main: term, producing a genuine efficiency-versus-capacity trade-off
2026-09-04 18:40:29 [INFO   ] main: that can be explored during multi-objective optimization.
2026-09-04 18:40:29 [INFO   ] main: Caveat: the loss coefficients are calibrated from a small set of
2026-09-04 18:40:29 [INFO   ] main: experimental systems (see loss_model.py). The qualitative trends
2026-09-04 18:40:29 [INFO   ] main: are physically motivated, while the exact sensitivity magnitudes
2026-09-04 18:40:29 [INFO   ] main: should be interpreted in light of the available calibration data.
